
  - [1mA. Filter panel above the table, always open.[0m A date-range Select plus all nine event types as checkboxes. You can
    see and reach everything directly, but it pushes the table down by about four lines.
  - [1mB. Compact bar with event types in a popover.[0m Takes one line, but finding failed sign-ins means opening the popover,
    clearing all, and checking one box.
  - [1mC. Two single-value Selects.[0m The simplest, and "Failed sign-ins" is one pick, but you can't combine types. It would
    also need group names (new copy for reviewers to check).

  I lean towards [1mA[0m. It keeps failed sign-ins one interaction away, which is what Security asked for, and it uses only
  the Select and Checkbox-list components the guidelines already specify. B saves space but hides the filter people most
  need.

  Pick an option in the browser or reply here. Separately, the sketches are saved under [38;5;153m.hyperpowers/[39m in the repo, which
  isn't in [38;5;153m.gitignore[39m. I won't commit it, but you may want to ignore it.

